# Local working state, never repository content.
#
# A git worktree checked out under .claude/worktrees/ presents a second copy of
# every file the rules above exclude, at a path those root-anchored rules do not
# match — so `pnpm check` failed on directories that are not part of the tree
# being checked. Scoped to worktrees/ rather than all of .claude/, so a tracked
# .claude/settings.json or agent definition is still formatted.
#
# .remember/ is separate: it is agent session state that no ignore file covers,
# so Prettier walked it too.
.claude/worktrees/
.remember/

